# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the C unit-test ASan lane
# (make test-unit-c-asan-tape). Wired in via LSAN_OPTIONS in mk/tests.mk.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: lsan_teardown.c already frees everything
# the tape/arena legitimately own (op_meta, non-persistent grads, arena
# chunks) before LSan's exit check, so the only records left are tape's
# genuinely-unfreeable-on-tape *persistent* allocations. On tape
# `tensor_free` is a no-op (the tape holds non-owning pointers), so a
# persistent tensor created by a bare unit test has no safe per-tensor
# free path — it lives until process exit by design (see
# create_scalar.c, param_create.c, design-decisions.md "Pluggable
# Device"). Each entry matches the allocation site; LSan also suppresses
# the indirect children (the tensor's data/shape/grad) hanging off it.
#
# These match the renamed tape symbols (…_tape) by substring.

# Persistent 0-rank scalars — always persistent=1 (create_scalar.c).
leak:tensor_create_scalar

# Persistent learnable params (1d/2d, f64/f32) — param_create.c.
leak:tensor_create_param

# Persistent non-learnable state (NTM/DNC) — param_create.c.
leak:tensor_create_state

# Persistent f32 params/state via the dtype-streamed path — dtype_dispatch.c.
leak:tape_persistent_f32_from_doubles

# Test-helper buffer handed to tensor_create_*_f32, which routes to the
# f32-unsupported tape stub (per_dtype_legacy.c) that returns without
# consuming its input. Test-only (heap_copy in port_assert.h, used by the
# split per-area C suites).
leak:heap_copy
